  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Waving My Dick In The Wind** (1 other source): A small cut near the end of this song was covered with a crossfade in the transfer [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Ween2008-07-09d1t02 Don't Shit Where You Eat**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Ween2008-07-09d1t05 Learnin' To Love**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Waving My Dick In The Wind**: cut on the recording [2]\n- **Audience**: rare: 7 archived performances [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **Ween2008-07-09.nakamichi** (recommended): source not stated; 31 songs; 158 min [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **Ween2008-07-09.nakamichi**: Recorded with Nakamichi CM700 mics and CP701 capsules into a Lunatec V3 at 24-bit/48kHz, then an M-Audio MT24/96; Transferred via Digital Concepts CR-70R card reader into Sound Forge 8.0, normalized, dithered to 16-bit, resampled to 44.1kHz, tracked in CDWav, encoded to FLAC level 8 [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by Status Serigraph: [2008 Ween - Nashville Silkscreen Concert Poster by Print Mafia](https://www.jojosposters.com/products/2008-ween-nashville-silkscreen-concert-poster-by-print-mafia) [3]",
